# For one kind, K = 1, the generator of D[kind-pairs] writes the windows of
# #795 at 004a0735: its segments 0, 1, 2 are WW, SW and SS. The references, Inputs/kind-pairs/*-795.windows, are #795's
# windows for the same controls; compare_segment_windows.py compares the
# values that each body yields as expressions, after renumbering (the
# order of operations and repeated constants aside), with the segment,
# cutoff, gathered fields, block arguments and result of each window.
#
# TIP3P with two ions: the same, with no exception.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/tip3p %t/opc
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/kind_pairs_tip3p.py %S/Inputs/triclinic %t/tip3p --solutes
# RUN: mdir emit --stage=module %t/tip3p/control.toml > %t/tip3p.mlir
# RUN: mdir-kind-pairs-test generate %t/tip3p/control.toml %t/tip3p.mlir 1 0.09582 > %t/tip3p-kinds.mlir
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/compare_segment_windows.py %S/Inputs/kind-pairs/tip3p-795.windows %t/tip3p-kinds.mlir | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TIP3P
#
# TIP3P: @energy sum segment(0, 0): 18 yielded values, the same expressions
# TIP3P: @energy sum segment(1, 0): 6 yielded values, the same expressions
# TIP3P: @energy sum segment(1, 1): 2 yielded values, the same expressions
# TIP3P: identical: 9 windows
#
# For OPC the same, with one constant replaced. The extra point's weight on each
# hydrogen is D403's, 0.14772060947071208, where #795 formed
# alpha = 0.14772060947071211 from the lengths; they differ by one unit in
# the last place. 18 occurrences: 9 windows' alpha and the 9 constants of
# the six windows that form the site twice (WW) or once (SW).
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/three.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/three.inpcrd %t/opc
# RUN: sed -e 's/TOPOLOGY/three.prmtop/' -e 's/COORDINATES/three.inpcrd/' %S/Inputs/kind-pairs/opc-run.toml > %t/opc/run.toml
# RUN: mdir emit --stage=module %t/opc/run.toml > %t/opc.mlir
# RUN: mdir-kind-pairs-test generate %t/opc/run.toml %t/opc.mlir 1 0.087343313000000005 > %t/opc-kinds.mlir
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/compare_segment_windows.py %S/Inputs/kind-pairs/opc-795.windows %t/opc-kinds.mlir 0.14772060947071211=0.14772060947071208 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OPC
#
# OPC: replaced 0.14772060947071211 by 0.14772060947071208 in the reference: 18 times
# OPC: @energy sum segment(0, 0): 20 yielded values, the same expressions
# OPC: @energy sum segment(1, 0): 8 yielded values, the same expressions
# OPC: @energy sum segment(1, 1): 2 yielded values, the same expressions
# OPC: identical: 9 windows
#
# Without the replacement the comparison fails at the first window that
# forms the site.
# RUN: not %python %S/Inputs/compare_segment_windows.py %S/Inputs/kind-pairs/opc-795.windows %t/opc-kinds.mlir 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WEIGHT
# WEIGHT: @energy sum segment(0, 0): the yielded expressions differ
